ig":"the crack tip for β = 0 . The greater the positive β is, the higher the reduction is. Similar to Fig. 4, all curves show slightly wavy patterns due to the impact of the density-dependent moduli.","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":742.2686492484376,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":72.0,"r":523.2796320999996,"t":765.4513845484374},"charspan":[0,194],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/0","text":"the crack tip for β = 0 . The greater the positive β is, the higher the reduction is. Similar to Fig. 4, all curves show slightly wavy patterns due to the impact of the density-dependent moduli."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"caption","orig":"Figure 6: T 22 vs. r ( T 22 unit: 10 4 Pa). In the first panel, at r = 0 (the crack-tip), negative β does not reduce T 22 compared with T 22 at β = 0 . Generally, a more negative value does not necessarily generate greater T 22 at the crack tip. In the second panel for β > 0 , positive β generates smaller T 22 value compared with T 22 at β = 0 . Greater β creates smaller T 22 at r = 0 . Slightly wavy patterns also appear in all the curves due to the effect of the density-dependent moduli.","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":496.02627024843736,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":71.99999999999994,"r":523.2773813599998,"t":564.1211200484374},"charspan":[0,493],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/1","text":"Figure 6: T 22 vs. r ( T 22 unit: 10 4 Pa). In the first panel, at r = 0 (the crack-tip), negative β does not reduce T 22 compared with T 22 at β = 0 . Generally, a more negative value does not necessarily generate greater T 22 at the crack tip. In the second panel for β > 0 , positive β generates smaller T 22 value compared with T 22 at β = 0 . Greater β creates smaller T 22 at r = 0 . Slightly wavy patterns also appear in all the curves due to the effect of the density-dependent moduli."},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"text","orig":"(a)","parent":{"$ref":"#/pictures/0"},"pro